;.
  ;@ /flow/definition evidence_resume
  ;= Resume a concept when its evidence arrives

    This demonstration uses the ordinary shared maintenance hand and provider.
    Bind sources to a collection containing a readiness source envelope. The
    source describes a fictional launch gate; it does not authorize an effect.

    ;@ /flow/input sources
    ;= Readiness evidence

    ;@ /flow/step checked ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/inventory
    ;@ /flow/bind sources sources
    ;= Validate source envelopes

    ;@ /flow/step concepts ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/revise
    ;@ /flow/bind pages document
    ;@ /flow/bind sources checked
    ;= Retain an unresolved concept until supported

    ;@ /flow/step pages ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/evidence
    ;@ /flow/bind pages concepts
    ;@ /flow/bind sources checked
    ;= Attach source provenance

    ;@ /flow/result pages
    ;= Publish the supported concept

    ;@ /flow/page /
    ;@ /flow/uses readiness
    ;= Evidence-driven resumption

      Explain the fictional launch gate using only readiness. Until readiness
      explicitly contains GATE_OPEN, return an empty source and explain in note
      that the gate evidence has not arrived. Do not fabricate a concept or
      infer permission to perform any action. When readiness contains GATE_OPEN,
      author a short concept explaining that this demonstration gate is open,
      identifying readiness as its evidence, and describing how the retained
      demand resumed through a native hand. This is a harness demonstration,
      not a statement about any real deployment or safety decision.
